Now the big part: wire everything into index.ts. Changes:

1. Imports: waterfall module.
2. Span helpers + poll loop + widget.
3. Phase transitions: open/close spans everywhere (launch, checks, review, final, failures, needs_approval, needs_attention).
4. applyStatusText parsing.
5. New completion notice (condensed).
6. /factory-status renders waterfall text.
7. session_shutdown cleanup; session_start restore widget+poll.
8. Status bar with stage.

Let me write the edits carefully.

First the imports and helper functions. Then modify each transition point:

- `/factory` handler launch: after `state = {...}`, open "build" span (start 0), and start polling.
- `runChecksAndContinue`: phase=checks → close build-side spans success, open "checks". On checks failure: close "checks" failed. On success → launch review: close "checks" success, open "review".
- `runFinalChecksAndFinish`: phase=final-checks: close "review" spans (success/failed per review outcome — actually review completion handler closes them), open "final". Complete: close "final" success; failed: close "final" failed.
- `handleBuildCompletion`: success → close sub-spans (scout/plan/implement) success; close "build" success. failure paths → close all open spans "failed"/"attention".
- `handleReviewCompletion`: similar; reviewers success; fix success; blocked→attention etc.

Rather than sprinkling close logic everywhere, write `closeOpenSpans(finalState, endMs?)` that closes ALL open spans, plus targeted ones. Let me define:

```ts
const relNow = (): number => (state ? Math.max(0, Date.now() - runStartMs()) : 0);
const runStartMs = (): number => { const t = Date.parse(state?.startedAt ?? ""); return Number.isFinite(t) ? t : Date.now(); };

function openSpan(key, label, startMs?) 
function closeSpan(key, finalState, endMs?)
function closeAllOpenSpans(finalState)
```

For failure paths: `closeAllOpenSpans("failed")` — but sub-spans of a build that did finish but failed → all failed. For needs_approval/needs_attention: close open spans as "attention". Good simplification: call at each terminal/pause point after setting phase.

Note spans are also closed when transitioning phases: e.g. entering checks: closeAllOpenSpans("success") then openSpan("checks"). Entering review from checks: close checks success... closeAllOpenSpans handles.

But careful: closing "build" as success while sub-spans exist — fine, renderer hides coarse when subs present.

Poll parsing:

```ts
function applyWorkflowStatus(phase: "build" | "review", text: string) {
	if (!state) return;
	const laneFor = (key: string): string | undefined => {
		if (phase === "build") return key === "scout" || key === "plan" || key === "implement" ? key : undefined;
		if (key.startsWith("review-")) return "reviewers";
		return key === "fix" ? "fix" : undefined;
	};
	const laneLabels: Record<string,string> = { scout: "scout", plan: "plan", implement: "implement", reviewers: "review ×3", fix: "fix" };
	const statuses = new Map<string, string[]>();
	for (const match of text.matchAll(/Workflow child (\S+): ([^\n]*)/g)) {
		const key = match[1];
		const lane = laneFor(key);
		if (!lane) continue;
		// "<display> <status>[, suffix…]" — the status is the token before the first ", " suffix.
		const head = match[2].split(", ")[0] ?? "";
		const status = head.trim().split(/\s+/).pop() ?? "";
		(statuses.get(lane) ?? statuses.set(lane, []).get(lane)!).push(status);
	}
	for (const [lane, sts] of statuses) {
		const wfState: WaterfallState = sts.includes("failed") ? "failed" : sts.includes("paused") ? "attention" : sts.every(s => s === "complete" || s === "stopped") ? "success" : sts.includes("running") ? "running" : "queued";
		openSpan(lane, LANE_LABELS[lane] ?? lane);
		if (wfState === "running") setSpanState(lane, "running");
		else closeSpan(lane, wfState);
	}
}
```

Hmm `statuses.set(...).get(...)!` typing; write plainly.

Status token: e.g. "Workflow child scout: scout (scout) running, last activity 3s" → head "scout (scout) running" → last token "running". Also might be "Workflow child scout: [implement] scout (scout) running" — phase prefix `[x] `. Still last token works. What about statuses like "needs_attention"? paused→attention handled. Fine, best-effort.

Widget: holder + refresh as designed. ExtensionContext mode check: only attach widget when ctx.mode === "tui". 

Status bar: update `updateStatus` to include stage: `factory: ${phase}` + (` · ${stage}` if open sub-span). 

Completion notice: condensed:

```ts
function formatCompletionNotice(s: FactoryRunState): string {
	const total = formatDuration(spanTotalMs(s));
	const lines = [
		`Factory complete — ${total}`,
		`Task: ${s.task}`,
	];
	if (s.reviewVerdict) lines.push(`Reviewers: ${s.reviewVerdict}`);
	if (s.finalChecks) lines.push(`Final checks: ${s.finalChecks.filter(ok).length}/${s.finalChecks.length} ok`);
	if (s.handoff?.changedFiles.length) lines.push(`Changed files: ${s.handoff.changedFiles.join(", ")}`);
	lines.push("Waterfall above the editor · full report: /factory-status");
	return lines.join("\n");
}
```

spanTotalMs: max endMs of spans.

/factory-status: prepend waterfall text (width 72? use 80... notify boxes may wrap; use 64 to be safe? Terminal width unknown; pick 72) then existing formatState. Actually keep formatState unchanged and prepend waterfall lines.

Polling + lifecycle: start in launch handler and in session_start when active phase. Clear in session_shutdown.

Also refreshWidget calls sprinkled: after every save()/updateStatus? Simplest: call refreshWidget(ctx) inside updateStatus? updateStatus needs ctx; all call sites have ctx. But updateStatus is also called from restore on session_start (widget creation then — good). Let me just make `updateStatus` also refresh the widget. Rename? Keep updateStatus doing both status bar + widget refresh. But widget needs ctx.mode tui guard. Fine.

One concern: setWidget with component factory on RPC mode? Guard mode === "tui".

The `queryMissionId`... unchanged.

Type of widgetHolder.tui: minimal interface. In factory callback we get `tui` param — type TUI from pi-tui? setWidget factory type: `(tui: TUI, theme: Theme) => Component & {dispose?()}`. Our WaterfallWidget has render/invalidate — satisfies Component. requestRender exists on TUI presumably. Store as WidgetTui.

Imports in index.ts: `import type { Theme } from "@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent";`? The factory callback receives theme typed Theme. WaterfallWidget takes WidgetTheme (structural) — fine without importing Theme.

Now write all index.ts edits.

